  - id: day_of_the_lord_2peter
    displayName: New Heavens and a New Earth
    flavorText: Peter answers the scoffers who doubt Christ's promised return, teaching
      that with the Lord one day is as a thousand years, that the day of the Lord
      will come as a thief in the night dissolving the heavens with fire, and that
      believers look for new heavens and a new earth wherein dwelleth righteousness.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Answers scoffers in the last days who doubt the promise of Christ's
      coming while walking after their own lusts, explains that with the Lord one
      day is as a thousand years and God's seeming slowness is longsuffering toward
      repentance, and describes the day of the Lord coming as a thief in the night
      in which the heavens and elements shall be dissolved with fire - grounding
      the promise of new heavens and a new earth 'wherein dwelleth righteousness'
      and exhorting believers to holy living and diligence to be found in peace,
      without spot, and blameless.
    deliveredByManagerId: peter_2peter
    managerId: day_of_the_lord_2peter
